1. KubeTrail (Apache-2.0) — ported (independent reimplementation)

   KubeTrail — https://github.com/ekkoo-z/KubeTrail — Apache License 2.0,
   Copyright the KubeTrail Authors. The repository README footer says
   "MIT License" but the LICENSE file is the authoritative Apache-2.0 text;
   this discrepancy is noted for honesty.

   InkBlade includes an independent Python reimplementation of selected
   KubeTrail capabilities under `inkblade/kubetrail/`:

   - in-pod collectors (identity/environment/serviceaccount/proc/proc_sys_escape/
     filesystem/node_local/runtime_local/k8s_context/k8s_permissions/
     credential_sweep/cloud_metadata/syscalls);
   - legacy ServiceAccount token audit (JWT decode without signature
     verification, expiry/audience/permission/default-SA risk);
   - sensitive-value tri-state storage (raw / redact / metadata);
   - manifest and ConfigMap cloud-key scanning;
   - Linux LPE heuristics (16-CVE version-range table, no exploit code);
   - persistence detection for the seven KubeTrail template classes.

   No Go source code from KubeTrail is copied, linked, or embedded; the port is
   an independent Python reimplementation of observable behavior and public
   documentation. Upstream copyright and Apache-2.0 attribution are retained
   here, in `docs/KUBETRAIL-PORT.md`, and in each `inkblade/kubetrail/*.py`
   header. `LICENSE` contains the full Apache-2.0 text; modified/derived files
   are marked. See `tools/check-notices.py` for the automated check.

